    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="8" relname="span">All of these concepts but the "Error recovery" can be measure by subjective means.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="11" relname="concession">The way we perform the evaluation of "ease of use","ease of learning","efficiency","memorability","user satisfaction","flexibility",and "consistency" are stablishing scales factors and having different people express their feelings about the software application evaluating them and scoring them.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="12" relname="span">But software applications as any other products have a "cost of opportunity" and a "level of satisfaction" (like in economy).</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="3" relname="elaboration">The cost of opportunity means if the user can have a different product than the one he has,</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="12" relname="elaboration">and the level of satisfactions is how comfortable the user feels about the software application.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="7" relname="concession">All the measures will be relative because of the different point of views of the humans evaluators,</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="13" relname="span">but at least we can measure them.</segment>
        <group id="8" type="span"/>
        <group id="9" type="span" parent="1" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="10" type="span" parent="9" relname="span"/>
        <group id="11" type="span" parent="10" relname="span"/>
        <group id="12" type="span" parent="11" relname="span"/>
        <group id="13" type="span" parent="10" relname="summary"/>
    </body>
</rst>
